{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S31-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d7c6615990e0fc3462f38c8d78fde519c25a280bb7c97b6e487399f4979b924c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 assigns familiar mugs and washing roles; A5's 'replacement' shifts toward protecting B's job rather than continuing their shared habit.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 accommodates B2's dishwasher with towels; B4 removes drying, prompting A5's supervision role.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 introduces a purchase that removes shared work, and B4 explains why A's proposed towel duty is unnecessary.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 invents another role for B but weakens the specific wash-and-dry routine established in A1.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's 'Your chipped mug, my ugly mug' immediately establishes domestic familiarity and a playable task.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'while it learns' economically expresses A's resistance to replacing a familiar arrangement.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 79\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your chipped mug, my ugly mug. I'll wash; you dry.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I bought a dishwasher.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Lovely. You load your side; I'll load mine.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"There's only one mug rack.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yours on the left, then. Pass me mine when it's done. We always put them away together.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A immediately applies shared shorthand and established habits to present arrangements, even when those arrangements have changed.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Fear of being replaced.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 divides the mugs through familiar shorthand; the revision's A3 and A5 preserve their customary sides and shared putting-away routine without demanding indispensability.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a preserves domestic cooperation through a new appliance; b translates a friend's familiar arrival signal into new communication methods.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original passed both causal links but drifted from routine into replacement. The revision keeps the kitchen setting: B4's single rack makes A5 recreate familiar sides and extend the habit to putting mugs away. Internal reread scores, in rubric order: 5/5/4/4/5/4 = 92. A1 supplies familiarity; B2/A3 and B4/A5 remain causal; B's practical constraints reshape cooperation; A5 extends the habit; the mugs anchor play; the final line earns its warmth through shared work.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The revised ending offers gentle recognition more than a sharp laugh; its established putting-away habit is newly specified illustrative history.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S31-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"6e2fc405a3e1c2cf6297f3fe6ffff52aa2c690b855d6ccd03c9be63745c7a90b\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 assumes the usual walk and two-knock signal; A3 and A5 carry that signal into doorbell and text.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's doorbell directly produces A3's two rings; B4's request for a text produces A5's textual knocks.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 has changed the arrival arrangement and B4 asks for advance contact, giving B a credible preference for less intrusive visits.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 preserves a physical knocking convention 