nomical, and A5's phone question follows the alert claim without explanation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've reminded you about the dentist tomorrow.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's in my calendar.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good. I'll remind you to check the calendar.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It sends alerts.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"To which phone? The one you asked me to find?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A supplies unsolicited reminders and tracks the failures of remembering as an established personal burden.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Controlling practical care.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 reminds B to consult the calendar rather than making the appointment or choosing for B; A5 remembers the phone problem.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a challenges automated safeguards through remembered dependence; b develops an increasingly intrusive physical reminder system.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The calendar and its alerts each give A a new, specific reminder failure to anticipate. Unchanged internal reread confirms 90 and all hard gates.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The phone may already have been found; A5 works as a pointed reminder of past dependence, not proof that alerts cannot work.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S33-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"3127818a4a42da935ff3b7dd25c955aeaf68d1f926046e86c5d569e170e04c48\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies an unsolicited bin reminder and A5 relocates it, but A3 treats an uneaten banana as evidence of forgetting bin day.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4's lack of hunger reasonably motivates A5's coffee-machine placement; B2's remembered bin day does not explain A3's banana test.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 asserts competence and B4 explains the untouched food, giving A resistance grounded in ordinary habits.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 changes reminder location but adds little commitment or consequence beyond A1's original method.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's writing on a breakfast banana gives the domestic routine an immediately playable, distinctive object.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 efficiently answers the appetite objection, but A3's joke relies on a questionable inference.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 75\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Bin day tomorrow. I've written it on your breakfast banana.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I don't always eat breakfast.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Right. I'll put another reminder on the coffee machine. Apparently I track breakfast now too.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll set a phone alarm. You can stop leaving notes.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good. I'll leave one by your charger reminding you what the alarm means.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A supplies unsolicited reminders and tracks the failures of remembering as an established personal burden.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General fussing over another person's habits.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 tracks breakfast only to deliver the bin reminder, and A5 adds a reminder explaining B's alarm rather than taking over the bin task.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This version adapts physical notes to B's proposed automation; a uses remembered phone trouble to question automation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original's B2/A3 link confused eating with remembering. The 