kes A5 discount time already awake and claim interrupted sleep. Internal reread: 5/4/4/4/4/4 = 86. A1/A5 make winning explicit; B2 and B4 each cause revaluation; B defends real labor; A5 adds a scoring category; the bus grounds the comparison; the final column completes A's biased calculation.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's sleep argument is deliberately self-serving; its logic must remain recognizable rather than merely nonsensical.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S35-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"cc412f53cb9aec8ff8f55de4ba04f0578c1496acdd0ed0d47008bdd0270490f3\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 asks for routine knowledge under a checking pretext, and A3 recasts B's answer as B passing a memory test.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 takes up B2's established counter; A5 explains away the mistaken direction exposed by B4.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 supplies useful local knowledge and B4 challenges A's pretense by naming the toilets A was approaching.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 expands a simple information check into a supposed inspection of misleading signs after B4 exposes actual confusion.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's forms and B2's counter three establish a public-service routine without exposition.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Good. You remember' efficiently reverses who needed help; A5 maintains that cover through the signs.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Which counter takes these forms? Just checking they've not moved it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's been counter three for years.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good. You remember.\"},\n        {\"speaker\"